Jon Myers writes:
 > Is there any way to get at sio1?  upon bootup, I always get "sio1: reserved 
<..>

Remove the flags from sio1 in your config file & rebuild your
kernel.

Eg:

Index: GENERIC
===================================================================
RCS file: /home/ncvs/src/sys/alpha/conf/GENERIC,v
retrieving revision 1.71.2.25
diff -u -r1.71.2.25 GENERIC
--- GENERIC     12 Oct 2002 15:25:07 -0000      1.71.2.25
+++ GENERIC     3 Mar 2003 22:06:57 -0000
@@ -122,7 +122,7 @@

 # Serial (COM) ports (required)
 device         sio0    at isa? port IO_COM1 irq 4
-device         sio1    at isa? port IO_COM2 irq 3 flags 0x50
+device         sio1    at isa? port IO_COM2 irq 3

 # Parallel port
 device         ppc0    at isa? irq 7


This is left over from using sio1 for kernel debugging years ago.
I'll see if I can get it yanked before the next release.  Its already
gone in -current.

 > Any ideas/suggestions?  Alpha 800.. 5/333  4.8-PRERELEASE  (umm.. I thought 
 > I was running -STABLE?  tag=RELENG_4)

-STABLE *is* 4.8-PRELREASE.  It will branch at the time of the
release, until then, its RELENG_4.

Drew


